




                            CE5 Programming Manual
				  Version 4.1


	 The CE5 (Clone/Editor 5) is used to program the Vertex series
    radios (4/12/24 channel). The radio is connected to the computer by
    using the FRB-2 programming interface box, or the VPL-1 and appro-
    priate cable.  To start the program, type the following at the DOS
    prompt:

         C:>CE5

	 The program will display the version number and frequency ranges
    for different model of radio then goes to main channel data screen.

	 The main channel data screen will allow you to enter all of the
    channel and tone data as well as set some of the programmable options
    like CTCSS, Time Out Timer, etc.  You can also access all of the other
    functions from the main screen by pressing one of the 'F' keys:

         F1:  On-line help
         F2:  Common Data/Hardware Setup
         F3:  Load a file from disk
         F4:  Save a file to disk
         F5:  Read data from a radio
         F6:  Send data to a radio
         F7:  Print out configuration
	 F8:  Return to DOS
         F9:  Change radio type

         The program starts with the default setting for FTL-2011 4 channel.
    To change the radio type use the F9 key and select using the up/down
    arrow keys and <SPACE>.  Press <ESC> to return to the main channel
    screen.  Changing types will erase any previous data on the screen.

         Two information boxes appear at the top of the screen.  The left
    box contains information about the common data and radio configuration.
    The box on the right contains key help information for data entry such
    as which keys to use and the upper and lower limits for data.

         Before programming the channel data, make sure that the COMMON
    DATA and ENVIRONMENT settings are correct. The following items can be
    entered from the channel data menu:

    PRIORITY CHANNEL-Up to 2 channels can be enabled as a priorities; use
    the <1> or <2> keys to select/de-select.

    CHANNEL NUMBER-This is the number that is displayed on the LED front
    panel for the 12/24 versions; it does not affect the 4 channel radio.
    Any number can be entered between 00-99 in any order.




					 1











    RX FREQ-Enter any frequency within the selected range (29.7-50 for
    Lo-Band, 134-174 for VHF 400-512 for UHF, and 806 to 870 for 800 Mhz)
    and channel spacing.  Pressing the <SPACE> bar will toggle the "channel
    lock" on or off; if locked, the channel data will not be displayed or
    accessed by the user, but will still be downloaded.

    CTCSS DECODE-Press <ENTER> to select the tone frequency from the CTCSS
    table, or press the <SPACE> bar to toggle CTCSS decode on/off.

    DCS DECODE-If an FDS-1 is installed, the radio is capable of DCS
    operation.  Press <ENTER>  to select the DCS code from the table, or
    press <SPACE> to toggle DCS decode on/off.  DCS is mutually exclusive
    with CTCSS (you cannot select both).

    BCLO-Press the <SPACE> bar to toggle between Busy Tone Lock Out, Busy
    Carrier Lock Out, and None.  BTLO will inhibit the transmitter if
    carrier is detected but the correct tone is not decoded.  BCLO will
    inhibit the transmitter anytime carrier is detected.

    SCAN-Press the <SPACE> bar to change the scan list selection for this
    channel.

    TX FREQ-Enter any frequency within the selected range (29-50 MHz for
    Lo-Band, 134-174 for VHF, 400-512 for UHF or 806-870 for 800 MHz) and
    channel spacing.  Pressing the <SPACE> bar will toggle the channel
    between receive only and TX/RX.

    CTCSS ENCODE-Press <ENTER> to select the tone frequency from the CTCSS
    table, or press the <SPACE> bar to toggle CTCSS encode on/off.

    DCS ENCODE-If an FDS-1 is installed, the radio is capable of DCS
    operation.  Press <ENTER>  to select the DCS code from the table, or
    press <SPACE> to toggle DCS decode on/off.  DCS is mutually exclusive
    with CTCSS (you cannot select both).

    TX POWER-Press the <SPACE> bar to toggle the channel between low power
    only, or HI/LO power (selectable by the user).  NOTE: FTL-1011 does not
    have low power available as an option.

    TX TIMER-Press the <SPACE> bar to toggle the TX Time Out Timer on/off.
    The timer duration is set under COMMON DATA.

    COMMON DATA

    Pressing <F2> will allow you to view/edit the radio common data.  All
    of the selections are altered using the <SPACE> bar.  The following
    items can be accessed from this menu:

    1.   Scan resume time; select either 5 Sec or CARRIER.  If set to
	 CARRIER, scan will resume 2 Sec after carrier drops. If set to 5
	 sec, scan will pause only for that time, then resume regardless of
	 activity.


					 2











    2.   Priority During Scan; enable or disable priority scanning.

    3.   Priority Scan Time; select either slow (1.5 Sec) or fast (.5 Sec).

    4.   Talk back; if enabled, radio will remain on channel when taken off
	 hook while scanning is stopped on a busy channel in order to allow
	 the user to respond to a call.  If disabled, radio will revert to
	 Home channel. HOME CHANNEL MUST BE ENABLED TO USE THIS FUNCTION.

    5.   Home channel; if enabled, radio will revert to home channel (chan-
	 nel selected before scanning started) anytime the mic is taken off
	 hook.  If disabled, radio will revert to Priority 1 when off hook.

    6.   Off Hook function can be enable or disabled.  If disabled, taking
	 the mic off hook does not put the radio in the monitor mode or
	 revert to off hook status as determined above.

    7.   Monitor button can be enabled or disabled.

    8.   TX Time Out Time; select 30 Sec to 7.5 min in 30 Sec increments,
	 or disabled.

    9.   Time Out Resume is the amount of penalty time that must expire
	 before the user can transmit again if they have exceeded the TOT.
	 Select either 0, 6, 20, or 60 Sec.

   10.   TX Carrier Delay can be enabled or disabled;  if enabled, releas-
	 ing the PTT button will cause the radio to continue to transmit
	 for 400 mSec without tone to eliminate the squelch tail on the
	 receiving end.

   11.   A key can be programmed for HI/LO power select, talk around (TX
	 freq is shifted to RX freq), Call (2-tone sel call reset and
	 unmute), or Accessory (used for future expansion).  On FTL-1011,
	 the A key can only be programmed for talk around, Call, Accessory,
	 and noise blanker (HI/LO power is not available).

   12.   2-Tone decoder; select either Motorola groups 1,2,3 or 4,5,6.
	 Selecting CUSTOM allows the user access to non-standard tones by
	 reprogramming the F2D-4 ROM at the factory with the proper data,
	 and selecting the tone number vs. tone frequency.

    SERIAL PORT

    Pressing <F4> in the COMMON DATA screen will allow you to change serial
    port if computer has more than one serial port.

    ENVIRONMENT

    The following items can be accessed by pressing <F2> while in the
    COMMON DATA menu.  The first 3 items can only be accessed if the
    program is started with the -P option (C:> CE5 -P).  Changing any of
    these 3 items requires hardware modifications to the radio and should

					 3











    not be altered from their default settings under normal conditions.
    Use the <SPACE> bar to toggle all of the ENVIRONMENT settings.

    1.   Prescalar: select 1/32 (default FTL-1011) 1/64 (default) or 1/128.

    2.   Channel step: select 5/6.25 or 10/12.5 kHz.  Default depends on
	 radio type.

    3.   1st IF Freq: Enter 00.00 to 99.99.  Default depends on radio type.

    4.   Local Osc Offset: select either higher or lower.  Default depends
	 on radio type.  If changed from default to eliminate image
	 problems, radio will need retuning and possible modification.  It
	 is not recommended to alter this setting in the field.

    5.   Default split is applied to the receive frequency to automatically
	 calculate the transmit frequency.  This setting does not affect
	 the operation of the radio.

    6.   Scan Speed: select 5 to 80 mSec in 5 mSec increments.  Default is
	 50 mSec.  SETTING THE SCAN SPEED TOO FAST MAY CAUSE MESSAGES TO BE
	 MISSED.

    7.   Memory Channel: select 4, 12, or 24 depending on the front panel
	 being used and the number of EEPROMS installed (24 Ch requires 2
	 chips).

	 To return to the COMMON DATA menu press <ESC>.


    2-TONE DECODE

	 Pressing <F3> from the COMMON DATA menu allows you to select the
    2-tone frequencies for decode.  Each channel may have a different tone
    pair, and the tone selections are based on the tone set selected under
    COMMON DATA (Motorola 1,2,3/4,5,6 or custom).  Custom tones must be
    programmed by the factory into the F2D-4 ROM and are selected by tone
    number rather than tone frequency.


    LOAD A FILE FROM DISK

	 To load a previously saved configuration from disk, press <F3>
    from the main channel menu.  A list of the current directory appears
    with all files that end in the ".CH" extension.  To change directories,
    or to search for other file extensions, enter the new path from the
    keyboard and press <ENTER> and a new list should appear.

	 To select the desired file, use the arrow keys, or type the full
    name plus extension and press <ENTER>.  The file must be of the correct
    type (UHF/VHF) or you will get an error message.



					 4











    SAVE A FILE TO DISK

         To save a configuration to disk, press <F4> from the main channel
    menu.  A list of the current directory appears with all files that end
    in the ".CH" extension.  To change directories, or to search for other
    file extensions, enter the new path from the keyboard and press <ENTER>
    and a new list should appear.  Enter the name and extension and press
    <ENTER> to save the file (file name and ext must be valid DOS types).

         To save a configuration as a previously saved file, select the
    desired file using the arrow keys, or type the full name plus extension
    and press <ENTER>.  You will be prompted before overwriting an existing
    file.


    READ A CONFIGURATION FROM THE RADIO

         Before any data can be read from the radio, it must be put into
    the clone mode.  Insert the cloning cable into the mic jack and turn
    the radio on.  The LED display should blink "CL" (12/24 channel) or
    LED #1 should be blinking (4 channel).  The radio is now ready to send
    data.

	 Press <F5> from the main channel menu and press the <SPACE> bar.
    Press the "A" button to begin uploading.  The YELLOW LED on the radio
    will blink to indicate data transfer.  The computer screen will indi-
    cate when reading is complete.

         The computer will prompt you to save the previously displayed
    channel information before overwriting the newly uploaded data to the
    screen.  If you wish to save the data, answer "Y" and enter a file name
    as above.


    PROGRAM A CONFIGURATION INTO THE RADIO

         Before any data can be read from the radio, it must be put into
    the clone mode.  Insert the cloning cable into the mic jack and turn
    the radio on.  The LED display should blink "CL" (12/24 channel) or
    LED #1 should be blinking (4 channel).  The radio is now ready to send
    data.

         Press <F6> from the main channel menu and press the <SPACE> bar.
    Press the "MON" button then the <SPACE> bar to begin sending; the
    YELLOW LED on the radio will flash to indicate data transfer. The
    computer screen will indicate when the download is complete.


    PRINTING

         Press <F7> from the main channel menu to print the configuration.
    The computer will prompt you to ready the printer and press "Y" to
    continue or any other key to abort.

                                         5











    QUIT to DOS

         Press <F8> from the main channel menu to quit CE5 and return to
    DOS.  Computer will ask you to confirm.


    RADIO TYPE

         Four types of radios can be programmed using the CE5 software:
    FTL-1011, FTL-2011, FTL-7011, and FTL-8011 (800 MHz still under de-
    velopment).  Press <F9> from the main channel menu to bring up the
    radio type menu.  Use the up/down arrow keys and the <SPACE> bar to
    select.  Changing radio types will erase all previous data.









































